course: dictionary
lesson: 6978
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Pantheon has more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one is meant. A pantheon is all the gods of a people or religion, taken together, or a group of the most famous or important people in an area. With a capital P, the Pantheon is a name for a famous building.
explain: Read this: «The Romans used arches, domes and concrete, and the Pantheon in Rome, nearly 1,900 years old, still has the world's largest unreinforced concrete dome.» The clues are Rome, nearly 1,900 years old and dome. These show the Pantheon is a building, not a group of gods.
explain: With a small p, pantheon usually means a group. The Greek pantheon is the whole set of Greek gods, and a fan who says a player has joined the pantheon of greats means that player is among the very best. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: A pantheon is all the gods of a people or religion, taken together.
fact: A pantheon can also be a group of the most famous or important people in an area.
fact: «The Pantheon» with a capital P is a famous ancient temple in Rome with a huge dome.
fact: There is also a building in Paris called the Pantheon, where famous French people are buried.
fact: A capital letter in the middle of a sentence often shows a name, such as a building or place.
exercise: In a history lesson, what does the Greek pantheon mean? | A Greek hero who fought in a long war | A famous Greek temple with a dome | *All the Greek gods, taken together | A Greek village by the sea
exercise: «The Pantheon in Rome, nearly 1,900 years old, still has the world's largest unreinforced concrete dome.» What kind of thing is the Pantheon here? | A type of cake | A group of gods | *A famous ancient building | A football team
exercise: A fan says a new player has joined the pantheon of greats. What does pantheon mean here? | A player who has just retired | A school for footballers | A player who has been sent off | *A player who is among the very best
test: «The Pantheon in Rome, nearly 1,900 years old, still has the world's largest unreinforced concrete dome.» Which word is the clue that the Pantheon is a building, not a group of gods? | *dome | world's | Romans | years
test: «The Pantheon is a famous ancient temple in Rome.» Which meaning fits the Pantheon here? | *A famous old building | A group of famous footballers | All the gods of a people | A type of marble
exam: Jayden meets pantheon and does not know which meaning is right. What should he do? | Skip every sentence with a hard word in it | Only read the capital letters | Ignore the whole sentence and guess | *Read the clue words around it, swap each meaning into the sentence, and check a dictionary if still unsure
